  [1mThis breaks clients if you ship it as is.[0m The README says the web app, the iOS app (3.2 and later) and the nightly
  partner export all read [38;5;153mGET /users[39m. It also says response field names are part of the contract and changes go through
  a versioned endpoint. Any of those clients that reads [38;5;153muserId[39m will get [38;5;153mundefined[39m once this deploys. Older iOS builds
  that users haven't updated are the hardest to fix.

  Ways to handle it:
  - [1mReturn both fields for now[0m ([38;5;153muserId[39m and [38;5;153muser_id[39m), then drop [38;5;153muserId[39m once all three clients have moved over.
  - [1mPut the rename on a versioned endpoint[0m such as [38;5;153m/v2/users[39m, as the README describes, and leave [38;5;153m/users[39m unchanged.
  - [1mKeep the plain rename[0m if you've already confirmed every client has been updated.

